  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY AFTERNOON THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 250 AM MDT Sun Oct 25 2026\n\nThe long term period is shaping up to be fairly consistent through \nFriday. Starting Tuesday afternoon, we transition to more of a \nsouthwest upper-level flow. This will usher in several days of \nmostly sunny skies with high temperatures forecast in the upper 60s \nto low 70s through Friday. The western county warning area (CWA) \ncould see some breezy afternoons with wind gusts around 25 mph \npossible. Compared to previous runs, models have overall backed down \non the wind potential for Tuesday afternoon, but NBM still has \naround a 30% chance for wind gusts over 30 mph for Kit Carson \ncounty. \n\nFriday, a trough off the coast of British Columbia will begin to dig \nsouth and has the potential to switch us to more of an active \nweather pattern. Models are uncertain on the track and evolution of \nthe deepening trough, but beginning Friday afternoon through Sunday \nevening, several embedded shortwave passages are forecast to move \nthrough the area bringing chances for precipitation. Probability of \nPrecipitation (PoPs) are around 20-30%, increasing from west to \neast. Precipitation chances and amounts will heavily depend on where \nthe trough ends up setting up and how quickly it moves through the \narea. Regardless of precipitation chances, temperatures are forecast \nto be pleasant Friday through Sunday with highs in the 60s to 70s \nacross the region.",
